":"ccg"},"ZZ880":{"name":"COUNTY COST GROUP 880","class":"ccg"},"ZZ890":{"name":"COUNTY COST GROUP 890","class":"ccg"}},"statuses":{"ok":{"label":"Benchmark available","text":"Every value shown is measured against this area's local benchmark."},"no_zori":{"label":"No rent benchmark","text":"Zillow publishes no rent index for any ZIP code in this MHA, so rent adequacy cannot be measured. The HUD Small Area Fair Market Rent cross-check is still shown."},"piti_only_no_zori":{"label":"Ownership cost without utilities","text":"This MHA has a home value but no Zillow rent index, so there is no utilities estimate. Buy values compare BAH with mortgage, property tax and insurance only, which overstates how far BAH goes."},"no_home_value":{"label":"No home-value benchmark","text":"Zillow publishes no home value index for any ZIP code in this MHA, so buy adequacy cannot be measured."},"ccg_no_benchmark":{"label":"BAH rate only","text":"This is a County Cost Group. DoD publishes no rent/utilities split for it and many of its rural ZIP codes have no rent index, so only its BAH rate is shown."},"no_rate":{"label":"No BAH rate","text":"These ZIP codes are in U.S. territories, where members receive Overseas Housing Allowance instead of BAH. DTMO lists them without a BAH rate."}},"caveats":{"ccg_geometry":{"title":"Approximate boundary","text":"DoD publishes no boundaries for County Cost Groups or the territory bucket. This outline joins the Census ZIP Code Tabulation Areas of the ZIP codes DTMO assigns to the area.","level":"area"},"outside_cluster_scope":{"title":"Outside the cluster analysis","text":"The spatial cluster analysis covers MHAs in the continental United States. This area is shown with its values but was not part of that analysis.","level":"area"},"ccg_no_benchmark":{"title":"No adequacy measure","text":"County Cost Groups have no local benchmark in this project, so only the BAH rate is shown.","level":"row"},"utilities_grossed_up":{"title":"Utilities estimated","text":"Zillow's rent index excludes utilities, while BAH covers rent plus utilities. The rent is grossed up with DoD's rent/utilities split for this MHA.","level":"row"},"piti_only_no_zori":{"title":"Utilities not included","text":"No utilities estimate exists for this MHA, so the ownership cost covers mortgage, property tax and insurance only.","level":"row"},"tax_insurance_locality":{"title":"Local tax and insurance","text":"Property tax is this MHA's effective rate from the Census American Community Survey (2020-2024). Insurance is the median premium per policy across its ZIP codes, from the Treasury Federal Insurance Office.","level":"row"},"tax_state_fallback":{"title":"State tax rate","text":"No local property-tax data was usable for this MHA, so the rate across its state's MHAs is used.","level":"row"},"insurance_state_fallback":{"title":"State insurance premium","text":"No ZIP code in this MHA has published insurance data, so the median premium across its state's MHAs is used.","level":"row"},"insurance_2022_dollars":{"title":"Insurance in 2022 dollars","text":"Insurance premiums are 2022 figures from the Treasury Federal Insurance Office, the latest published, used without adjustment. Premiums have risen since, so 2026 ownership costs are understated.","level":"row"},"type_factor_national":{"title":"National home-type adjustment","text":"No local Zillow series for this home type covers this area, so the difference between this home type and a typical home here uses the national ratio.","level":"row"},"lisa_exploratory":{"title":"Exploratory clusters","text":"Local clusters are shown where a test is significant at p < 0.05 without correcting for testing every MHA at once, so some are expected by chance. Areas outlined in black stay significant after a false-discovery-rate correction.","level":"overlay"}},"global_caveats":[{"id":"statutory_target","title":"How adequacy is measured","text":"By law, BAH equals the local cost of adequate housing minus a member cost share of 5% of the national average for the pay grade. An adequacy ratio of 1.00 means BAH plus that cost share exactly covers the local benchmark."},{"id":"market_rents","title":"Market rents, not DoD survey rents","text":"Local rent is the median of Zillow's rent index across the MHA's ZIP codes, a measure of typical asking rents for all homes. DoD's own survey prices specific dwelling types for each pay grade."},{"id":"benchmark_timing","title":"Benchmarks differ in timing","text":"BAH rates are for the BAH year shown, while each benchmark covers its own period. The data windows list the months and years used."},{"id":"zip_zcta_dropout","title":"Boundaries are approximate","text":"Area outlines are built from Census ZIP Code Tabulation Areas. PO-box and single-site ZIP codes have no tabulation area and are not drawn, although the areas they belong to still have outlines."},{"id":"home_type_benchmarks","title":"How home types are priced","text":"Rent: Zillow's typical rent for an area is taken to stand for a 2-bedroom townhouse, and other home types are scaled from it by the area's HUD Fair Market Rent bedroom ratios and by Zillow's multifamily or single-family rent against all homes. Zillow publishes those two rent series only by metro area, so the rent adjustment for building type is a metro-wide ratio. Buy: Zillow publishes no townhouse home values, so a townhouse is priced halfway between the area's condo and single-family values; apartments use condo values, and bedroom counts scale by Zillow's bedroom-count home values. Homeowners insurance is the area's average premium for every home type."}],"windows":{"bah_rates":"2026","rent_zillow_zori":"2026-01 to 2026-07","home_value_zillow_zhvi":"2026-01 to 2026-07","mortgage_rate_pmms":"2026-01 to 2026-07","rent_crosscheck_hud_safmr":"FY2026 (revised)","property_tax_acs":"2020-2024","insurance_fio":"2022"},"sources":[{"id":"A1","title":"BAH rates and ZIP-to-MHA assignments, 2026","provider":"Defense Travel Managemen